  "question": {
    "text": "Determine the current in $2 \\Omega$ resistor.\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/9LHP1mZg_THupKug7G8OcWj-yVsFw0ol27BuuiaIxdQ.original.fullsize.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "p8fGy",
      "text": "$1 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ulewa",
      "text": "$1.5 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "1Ps7R",
      "text": "$0.9 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5JU1n",
      "text": "$0.6 \\mathrm{~A}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "At steady state the capacitor will be fully charged and thus there will be no current in the $1 \\Omega$ resistance. So the effective circuit becomes\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/-IM_6Ce_QQBMUduk08aOH6hQKvdi7r4EThDa5QFH4lU.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nNet current from the $6 \\mathrm{~V}$ battery,\r\n\r\n$I=\\frac{6}{\\left(\\frac{2 \\times 3}{2+3}\\right)+\\frac{2.8}{1}}=\\frac{6}{1.2+2.8}=\\frac{3}{2}=1.5 \\mathrm{~A}$\r\n\r\nBetween $\\mathrm{A}$ and $\\mathrm{B}$, voltage is same in both resistances, $2 \\mathrm{I}_{1}=3 \\mathrm{I}_{2}$ where\r\n\r\n$\\mathrm{I}_{1}+\\mathrm{I}_{2}=\\mathrm{I}=1.5$\r\n\r\n$\\Rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{I}_{1}=3\\left(1.5-\\mathrm{I}_{1}\\right) \\Rightarrow \\mathrm{I}_{1}=0.9 \\mathrm{~A}$",
    "image": null
  },
